{
  "ID": "10",
  "Context/Background": "We leverage a clinical trial that compared neoadjuvant anti-PD-1 (Nivo), anti-PD-1+CTLA-4 (Nivo+Ipi), and anti-PD-1+LAG-3 (Nivo+Rela) therapies in head and neck squamous cell carcinoma patients. Combination therapies promote higher pathologic response rates versus monotherapy, and major pathologic response is associated with better survival. To address whether successful immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) regimens act through similar or distinct pathways, we robustly and longitudinally characterize transcriptional and proteomic dynamics of CD8+ tumor-infiltrating lymphocytes (TILs) in a clonal manner. \n\nThirty-eight patients were evaluable for pathologic tumor response (pTR) and categorized into three groups following previous studies: pTR-0 (91–100% viable residual tumor), pTR-1 (51%–90% viable residual tumor), and pTR-2 (≤50% viable residual tumor. \n\nTo study the association between transcriptional dynamics of T cells and pathologic responses to neoadjuvant ICI treatments, we isolated and profiled 372,914 CD45+CD3+ TIL from 35 patients (29 baseline and 31 post-surgical fresh tumor specimens; 20 patients having matched pre- and post-treatment biopsies), using the 10x Genomics 5′ scRNA-seq workflow. These cells were clustered into five distinct populations annotated as CD8+ T, CD4+ T, FOXP3+ T, γδ T/MAIT and cycling T cell clusters, and visualized by Uniform Manifold Approximation and Projection (UMAP) analysis. Clusters were annotated based on the expression of reported canonical T cell marker gene and CITE-seq expression levels.",
  "Prompt": "We analyzed the clusters of CD3+ TIL and found that the proportion of baseline CD8+ TIL showed a trend to the more frequent in responding patients.  When we assessed baseline expression of PDCD1, CTLA4, and LAG3 by CD8+ TIL, we observed the highest expression for PDCD1 and LAG3. The expression of PDCD1 and LAG3 by baseline CD8+ TIL positively correlated with the degree of pathologic response only in Nivo+Rela-treated patients. Similar analyses did not show a significant correlation between LAG3, PDCD1 and CTLA4 expression levels in baseline CD8+ TIL and the degree of pathologic response in the Nivo and Nivo+Ipi cohorts.\n\nTo identify baseline CD8+ TIL transcriptional signatures correlating with pathologic response, we generated a list of differentially expressed genes (DEG) between pTR-2 and pTR-0 tumors for each regimen.\n\nBased on the differentially expressed genes (DEGs) between pTR-2 and pTR-0 tumors for the Nivo+Ipi and Nivo+Rela cohorts, generate a summary describing the key transcriptional signatures, functional categories, and immune pathways enriched in pTR-2 vs pTR-0 tumors. Highlight representative genes and link them to their biological roles.  Focus on T cell–specific functional programs and gene modules defined by known immune states. ",
